move the wrapper fixture to the harness that runs it

The commit that fixed walkVisualErrors put its fixture in
testdata/test_error_under_wrappers.sngl, and nothing in the suite executes the
test functions there. `sngl test ./...` -- which is what `go tool verify` runs
-- does not walk testdata/, and no Go harness drives those files either: they
are type-checked by TestCheckTestdata and their assertions never run. The count
`go tool verify` prints did not move when the fixture was added, which is how
this was caught.

So it is a CLI script now, which is where CLAUDE.md puts anything that
*executes* a program. Both revert probes were redone against it: removing the
context-provider reach fails testRaiseUnderProviderIsCaught and not the other,
and removing the boundary's Failed walk fails testRaiseInFallbackIsCaught and
not the other.

Worth knowing beyond this fixture: every `testdata/test_*.sngl` in the
repository is in the same position. test_error_handling.sngl,
test_interp_types.sngl and the rest are checked and never run.

